{{Quote|First, some nice cold water! Then, I'll absorb the moisture from the air!|Waterhazard as he defeats [[Captain Nemesis|Overlord]].<ref name="HT">''[[Hero Time]]''</ref>}}
Waterhazard has the power of hydrokinesis, meaning he can control and manipulate all sources of ambient water,{{Refn|group = AP|name = Action}} including normal [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] water.{{Refn|[[:File:Water Hazard Can Manipulate Water.PNG]]|group = ES}}{{Refn|[[:File:Waterhazard Can Manipulate Water 2.png]]|group = DM}} This was first demonstrated by [[Bivalvan]], who changed the direction of his water blast to knock [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]] into some cables.<ref name="Fame">''[[Fame]]''</ref> Waterhazard has also used hydrokinesis to create water whips and to cushion [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]]'s fall.<ref name="RotS">''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]''</ref>

[[Orishan]] are particularly adept at extracting hydrogen and oxygen from the air and creating water out of it.{{Refn|group = AP|name = Action}} This allows Waterhazard to keep a steady supply of water in his body, which grants Waterhazard the ability to launch pressurized blasts of water through the portholes in his hands. With essentially the same kinetic energy as a fire hose, these blasts can be used to smash through walls, move large objects, and blast away enemies.{{Refn|group = AP|name = Action}} Waterhazard can use these same portholes to absorb water{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Escape From Aggregor]]''; [[:File:EFA DVD Water Hazard Data.png|file]]|group = DVD}} and moisture from the air.<ref name="HT">''[[Hero Time]]''</ref>

Waterhazard can jump exceptionally high.<ref name="RT">''[[Rook Tales]]''</ref> He can also use his water blasts to propel himself into the air.<ref>''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:Water Hazard Can Propel Himself.png]]|group = DR}}

Waterhazard is extremely durable, being able to withstand crashing into a wall seemingly painlessly.<ref name="BIM">''[[Bengeance is Mine]]''</ref> This is due to his incredibly tough, armored exoskeleton that protects his body and makes him nearly invulnerable to any physical attack.<ref>[[Ultimate Aggregor]]</ref><ref>''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''</ref>{{Refn|group = AP|name = Action}}

Waterhazard has enhanced strength, enough to throw [[Buglizard (Transformation)|Buglizard]] into a nearby wall<ref name="TMTCP2">''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref>
and punch craters into a concrete floor.<ref name="RT" />

Waterhazard's species is very clever and adept with technology, which allows him to build and repair complex machines, as demonstrated by Bivalvan.<ref name="Fame" />{{Refn|group = AP|name = Action}}

Waterhazard can breathe underwater.<ref name="Fame" />{{Refn|[[:File:Water Hazard Can Breathe Underwater.PNG]]|group = DM}} Waterhazard also can withstand radiation, such as that generated by a [[Prypiatosian-B]].<ref name="THtH">''[[Too Hot to Handle]]''</ref> However, he has been shown to be potentially hurt by the force of a Prypiatosian-B's radiation attack.<ref name="THtH" />

Waterhazard has a retractable visor hidden under his hood.<ref name="TT">''[[Tummy Trouble]]''</ref> His hood is also retractable.<ref name="TT" />{{Refn|[[:File:Retractable Hood.png]]|group = DJW}}

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Cosmic Destruction|Cosmic Destruction]]====
Water Hazard can create tornado and water whips as well as levitate/fly via water propulsion.
====[[Omniverse Collection]]====
Waterhazard is able to create a bubble shield around his body that protects him against lasers.

==Weaknesses==
Waterhazard is vulnerable to intense heat, such as that generated by a Prypiatosian-B.<ref>''[[Escape From Aggregor]]''</ref><ref name="THtH" /> He is also vulnerable to electricity, as demonstrated by [[Bivalvan]].<ref name="Fame" />

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Waterhazard's DNA was sampled and put in the [[Codon Stream]] when the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] scanned [[Bivalvan]]'s DNA.
*Waterhazard first appeared in ''[[Too Hot to Handle]]'', where he pretended to be Bivalvan in a failed attempt to convince [[P'Andor]] to go home. He was then defeated by P'Andor, prompting Waterhazard to switch into [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]].
*In ''[[Hero Time]]'', Waterhazard defeated [[Captain Nemesis|Overlord]].
*In ''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', Waterhazard briefly battled a [[Dr. Victor Valadis]] clone until it escaped.
*In ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', Waterhazard defeated [[Swamps]], but was defeated and frozen by [[Fridge]], so he switched into [[NRG]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Waterhazard was seen confronting [[Albedo]] in a dream.

===Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]'', Waterhazard battled [[Buglizard (Transformation)|Buglizard]] with [[Rook Blonko|Rook]]'s help.
*In ''[[Hot Stretch]]'', Waterhazard cooled off [[Ester]] and her friends.
*In ''[[Tummy Trouble]]'', Waterhazard sprayed [[Attea|General Attea]] off the [[Proto-TRUK]].
*In ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]'', Waterhazard "accidentally" incapacitated [[Will Harangue]], put out a fire accidentally caused by [[NRG]], and fought some [[Incursean (Classic)|Incursean]]s before the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]]'s randomizer function switched him into [[Astrodactyl]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Waterhazard failed to stop [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]] from getting the [[Polymorphic Crystal]].
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Waterhazard tried to break out of a force field but was reverted by the [[Forever Knights]]' DNA scanner.
*In ''[[For a Few Brains More]]'', Waterhazard defeated [[Ultimate Panuncian (Transformation)]].
*In ''[[Bengeance is Mine]]'', Waterhazard fought [[Sir Morton]] and the Forever Knights until [[Pakmar]]'s shop got flooded.
*In ''[[Rook Tales]]'', Waterhazard was defeated by [[Kundo]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Waterhazard appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

