==Etymology==
A water hazard is an area of water on a golf course designed to make it more difficult for players to get their ball onto the green.

==Trivia==
*Each of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s [[Andromeda (Classic)|Andromeda]] alien forms control a basic element. As his name suggests, Waterhazard commands water.
*Waterhazard is the first Andromeda alien Ben has scanned and used.
**[[Orishan|His species]] is also the first to be scanned by the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]].
*When Waterhazard first appeared in ''[[Too Hot to Handle]]'', his voice sounded exactly like [[Bivalvan]]'s did in ''[[Escape From Aggregor]]'' and ''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]'' because Waterhazard was supposed to be a clone of Bivalvan. Starting in ''[[Hero Time]]'', his voice became deeper to help differentiate him from Bivalvan.{{Refn|''link unavailable''|group = DM|name = voice}}
*Waterhazard was the [[Alien of the Month]] in January 2011.
[[File:Waterhazard and Ultimate Swampfire in Family Guy.png|thumb|Waterhazard figure in '''Family Guy''']]
*In the '''[[Wikipedia:Family Guy|Family Guy]]''' episode ''Quagmire and Meg'', during the scene where the old man is reading to his child, two toys that resemble Waterhazard and [[Ultimate Swampfire]] can be seen.
*Orishan have been confirmed to be separate entities from the [[Cascan]]s, another red hydrokinetic species from the Andromeda Galaxy that was introduced in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]]. [[Duncan Rouleau]] likens the differences between these species to those between [[wikipedia:Panther|panthers]] and [[wikipedia:Jaguar|jaguars]].{{Refn|[[:File:Orishan and Cascans Separate Species.png]]|group = DR}} or freshwater fish and saltwater fish.{{Refn|[[:File:Orishan and Cascans Separate Species 2.png]]|group = DR}}
**Duncan is a fan of both Waterhazard and [[Overflow (Reboot)|Overflow]] for different reasons, yet prefers the latter for his simplicity.{{Refn|[[:File:Duncan Likes Overflow.png]]|group = DR}}
**Unlike Cascans,{{Refn|[[:File:Overflow Extra Powers.png]]|group = DR}} Waterhazard cannot turn water into either ice or steam.{{Refn|[[:File:Water Hazard Cannot Turn Water Into Ice or Steam.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Duncan Rouleau believes that all canonical aliens from the [[Prime Timeline|Classic Continuity]] are in the Reboot Continuity Omnitrix,{{Refn|[[:File:Old Aliens Exist Proof.png]]|group = DR}}{{Refn|[[:File:Only Canon Aliens In Omnitrix.png]]|group=DR}}{{Refn|[[:File:RB Andromeda Aliens Added Later.png]]|group=DR}}, thus implying Waterhazard has a reboot counterpart.
*[[Ben 23]] has an alternate counterpart of Waterhazard.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Andromeda Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Years after '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' ended, [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] revealed that Ben 23's Orishan transformation was named Hose Hands.{{Refn|[[:File:Hose Hands Proof.png]]|group = DJW}} However, he declined to specify whether it was conceived during or after production.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Alien Names Revealed After Production.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Waterhazard was named by [[Marty Isenberg]], spelled "WaterHazard". The name was meant to be a placeholder but ended up being used as no one else came up with a better name.{{Refn|group = script|name = THTH Script}}
*Waterhazard was designed by [[Steven Choi]] for both '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' and '''Omniverse'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Steven Choi WH.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Waterhazard was originally not supposed to appear in:
**''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', with his role taken by [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/8/84/Revenge_of_the_Swarm_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Revenge of the Swarm'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}
**''[[Basic Training]]'', serving [[Terraspin]]'s role.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/31/Basic_Training_Draft-1.pdf ''Basic Training'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
**The dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/d/d4/Night_of_the_Living_Nightmare_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}

